Z||000000||extinct||12-21-2000||02:57 AM||||I have found an 88 formula, auto with sunroof.  The car has only 33,000 miles on it and has never been winter driven.  Everything works and needs nothing (yet!!)<BR>completely stock.  What would such a car be worth??<P>thanks||||reg||1
Z||000001||Old Lar||12-21-2000||09:02 AM||||If it is as nice as you say and the milage is that low, you may expect to pay $4-5 K. Its hard to say without looking at it, or driving it. Color: stock yellow is worth a little more.<P>Any car is worth what any one is willing to pay for it.||||reg||3
Z||000002||Fformula88||12-21-2000||05:20 PM||||I'd say its worth 5K or more.  If its as nice as you make it sound I'd pay that much.  Of course, check it over really good to be sure it wasn't in an accident or anything like that.  <P>------------------<BR>  <IMG SRC="http://www.geocities.com/formula2m6/FIEROSIG1.JPG">  <BR>1988 Fiero Formula||||reg||1
Z||000003||turbo86se||12-21-2000||05:30 PM||||It also depends on whether or not they're enthusiasts. If they aren't, you would have a better chance to get the car cheap, but if they know what it is, and how rare it is, they could ask more. I'd expect to pay 5-6K. Sounds nice, if you have the cash, go for it!<BR><P>------------------<BR> <A HREF="http://albums.photopoint.com/j/View?u=226077&a=5405885&p=20236431&Sequence=1&res=high" TARGET=_blank>http://albums.photopoint.com/j/View?u=226077&a=5405885&p=20236431&Sequence=1&res=high</A> ||||reg||1
Z||000004||DXR_DAD||12-21-2000||07:14 PM||||Old Lar is right, "ANY CAR IS WORTH WHAT ANY ONE IS WILLING TO PAY FOR IT"<P>What is the Kelly Blue on the car??<BR>When I'm looking to buy a classic/muscle car or collector type car I use as a price guide<BR>this book:  Standard Guide to Cars & Prices<BR>(Prices for collector Vehicles 1901-1992)<BR>James T. Lenzke & Ken Buttolph<BR>price ranges 1-6, 88 Formula 6,500 - 4,450 - 2,600 - 1,300 - 780 - 350<P>No.1 being in <B>show room condition!</B><BR>No.6 parts car<P>This is a good book to have<P>DXR_DAD<BR>||||reg||1
